They're not emergency rations, we're not at war.  These people have been asked to stay at home for their own safety and in return the government have been supplying them food to try and keep them from having any reason to go out.  By not even bothering to try and provide food they can eat though they're going to harm that effort.

&gt;You're talking about a government that can't even launch a tracing app correctly.

&gt; Expect people to receive the wrong packages.
&gt; 
&gt; Expect there to not be enough packages of the type that people want.
&gt; 
&gt; Expect accusations of deliberate and malicious insensitivity in both - where it's probably honest to goodness incompetence.
&gt; 
&gt; Expect fixing it to come at great cost to the taxpayer.

You're right, I don't expect them to be able to do something so basic but I think we should.  Having different packs for different religious dietary needs as well as vegetarian options isn't difficult for a supplier to arrange, it's literally just a list of items.
